Exception:
 if any unexpected event occurs, how Java handle the event and make the system smooth ti continue the normal flow

Object --->Throwable|---> Exception (these are recoverable) ---->Checked Exception
                    |               |
                    |               |--->Unchecked Exception
                    |
                    |
                    |
                    |----> Error eg. OutofMemoryError, StackOverFlowError (Developers dont handle errors)

Exceptions:
    --> Checked Exception
            --> checked at the compile time
    --> Unchecked Exception
            --> checked at the run time

finally:
    -->Always execute , irespective of error or happy flow

Throw:
    -->Keyword,explicitly create and throw an exception
    --> Syntax : throw new ExceptionType("Message")
    Imp Points:
        --> Used inside a method
        -->Throw only one exception at a time
        --> Followed by a exception object
        --> can throw both checked and unchecked exceptions

Throws:
    --> used in method declaration
    --> Syntax: accessspecifier returnType methodName() throws ExceptionType
